SELECT *
FROM (
  VALUES
    ('ios_crash_gate', 'iOS crash gate', 'blocked', 'Authenticated App Store Connect reports two crashes for public iOS 1.0.1 (4): one on 2026-08-25 and one on 2026-08-29. The 2026-08-29 event maps to iPhone; the 2026-08-25 device/OS dimension is suppressed or unavailable. Neither event exposes a diagnostic, stack, incident/signature ID, or crashed-binary UUID. Current product commit 2cdd4387fc2b8b0f4cd3e3a873f019a6ca8a3652 inherits preventive storage-failure hardening and tolerant optional Open-Meteo decoding; ordinary exact-source run 33300967788 passed shared Simulator tests and 18/18 Apple surface-state tests. Protected run 33381050098 now also provides a retained, independently byte-verified distribution-signed 1.1.0 (6) IPA/archive with matching profiles, entitlements, signatures, and dSYM UUIDs. That candidate is not the crashed public build, has not been uploaded or exercised through TestFlight, and cannot identify or be attributed to either production event. Diagnostic access and symbolication, an exact TestFlight physical iPhone/iPad/widget/watch pass, and post-rollout crash evidence remain missing.', 'Obtain and symbolicate any diagnostic Apple exposes, upload the exact retained IPA unchanged to TestFlight, complete the iPhone/iPad/widget/watch matrix, and collect post-rollout evidence'),
    ('open_meteo_promotion_clearance', 'Open-Meteo promotion clearance', 'pass', 'The complete authenticated Gmail record was checked read-only on 2026-08-29. The 06:05:07 +05:00 request described Nimbo as free and non-monetized, with no subscriptions, advertising, paid features, affiliate links, accounts, analytics SDK, or sale of user data, and limited promotion to unpaid localized posts, one personalized contact plus at most one follow-up, genuine Apple/Google editorial submissions, and ordinary unpaid links. At 17:25 +05:00, Nicoletta Addimando via OpenMeteo GmbH replied in ticket 234272 and explicitly confirmed that under those terms Nimbo is entitled to use the non-commercial API. This pass is limited to that exact scope and the published Free API limits; monetization, paid promotion, attribution removal, limit changes, or other material facts require a new licensing decision.', 'Preserve the confirmed scope and reopen licensing review before any material monetization, promotion, attribution, endpoint, or usage-limit change'),
    ('release_artifact_source_sync', 'Release artifact source sync', 'pass', 'Product/build-input commit 2cdd4387fc2b8b0f4cd3e3a873f019a6ca8a3652 resolves to Android phone 1.1.0 (8), Wear OS 1.1.0 (1000008), and Apple 1.1.0 (6). Exact-source ordinary GitHub Actions run 33300967788 passed Android/shared, Apple, and all 15 Compose UI tests across API 24 phone, API 36 phone, and API 36 tablet. Protected signing run 33381050098 produced the schema-v3 receipt-bound source-current set. Hosted materialization run 33392732428 retained the exact package and receipt in unpublished mutable draft release 379745439. A fresh local macOS verification reopened and rechecked the exact draft state and all 104 safely extracted files with pinned Bundletool 1.18.3. After successful current-master CI run 33404028777, protected workflow_run 33405849102 then completed the isolated no-checkout Ubuntu staging and separate read-only hosted macOS full verifier at b07192e91ae7f0f56ac3db7240383d7c53b94a2c. It revalidated live draft release 379745439 and asset IDs 537966386/537966414 before and after download and returned byte_verified=true for phone d4a90676f32745ea314b50ced2c9955e86923589534a1a7654ac6f1207e88a62, Wear e76d685b20e86f8878be7c9a1a59ac6edb5781ec8e61d5ecd36feb52ddc1cccf, and Apple 7466afb1a06f3000ad5d095734082d57cf58e992bdd7a8bed326e90d26ba39d0. Receipt artifact 9763131726 has GitHub digest 41e81e8c9f464dc2a0fe13c49697ae445285c77ef8e580f701fa29ad1ff74b3e. The committed manifest remains atomically 3/3 verified-current and draft-blocked because physical QA and store delivery are separate. The draft remains mutable, so the protected chain must recheck it before every later use; the required hosted repeat itself is complete. Evidence is growth/quality/release-artifact-full-verification-2026-08-31-hosted.md. No physical-device, TestFlight, Play internal, store upload, processing, review, publication, public availability, crash-gate, or ranking claim follows from this pass.', 'Require the protected hosted chain to recheck the mutable draft before every later use, then bind store-delivered physical QA without changing the promoted artifact bytes'),
    ('android_physical_smoke', 'Android device smoke', 'blocked', 'Product commit 2cdd4387fc2b8b0f4cd3e3a873f019a6ca8a3652 retains independently byte-verified upload-key-signed phone AAB d4a90676f32745ea314b50ced2c9955e86923589534a1a7654ac6f1207e88a62 and Wear AAB e76d685b20e86f8878be7c9a1a59ac6edb5781ec8e61d5ecd36feb52ddc1cccf. On 2026-08-31 the exact phone AAB was reopened with pinned Bundletool 1.18.3 and converted without rebuilding into upload-key-signed APK set 28ab80e1693a23586edfac76278409e7749ede4db476e67841ee61f6fa181752 and universal APK e970352d54e4c95100f03539c54dbecb0732c635e2f6057715215f271d24e976. APK Signature Schemes v2/v3 and upload certificate 431548a4871c9c090eee808ac3a34898f5d78602d9e747dfe81e228415aac252 verified. A clean physical General Mobile Android 7.1.1 / API 25 install reproduced the universal APK hash from pulled installed base.apk and passed Russian onboarding without location, live Tashkent forecast, Best Time Outside, native share chooser, proven-offline cached cold start and fallback warning, network recovery, and process-health checks before cleanup. An independent com.android.vending native abort during sideload was isolated to the old Play Store process; Nimbo remained alive. This closes only the local exact-AAB-derived phone scope. Play app-signing-key internal delivery, a Play-delivered phone rerun, physical tablet/widget coverage, and paired physical Wear OS coverage remain missing. The Samsung API 36 device still contains user data and is not overwritten. No Play upload, processing, internal-track assignment, public rollout, vitals, or availability is claimed. The gate remains blocked.', 'Deliver the exact phone and Wear AABs through Play Internal, rerun the phone scope against the Play-delivered package, and complete physical tablet/widget and paired Wear OS QA'),
    ('ios_physical_smoke', 'iOS physical smoke', 'blocked', 'Historical product commit 9c2dce4200dbba5487c8c458ade4616005fde6e6 retains simulator-only Apple evidence that does not transfer to current authority 2cdd4387fc2b8b0f4cd3e3a873f019a6ca8a3652. Twelve targeted current-source iOS Simulator provider tests and exact-source hosted Apple regression tests pass. Protected run 33381050098 provides retained, independently byte-verified distribution-signed IPA 7466afb1a06f3000ad5d095734082d57cf58e992bdd7a8bed326e90d26ba39d0 plus matching xcarchive, app/widget/watch profiles, entitlements, signatures, and dSYM UUIDs for 1.1.0 (6), and trusted hosted run 33405849102 repeated the full verifier successfully. Because the IPA uses App Store profiles, direct devicectl installation is invalid; exact runtime proof must use that unchanged upload through TestFlight. The iPhone 14 Pro on iOS 26.6.1 and iPad mini 5 on iPadOS 26.6 are paired, booted, Developer Mode enabled, and suitable for a TestFlight update and fresh install respectively after processing. The paired Series 5 watch on watchOS 10.6.2 is compatible, but Developer Mode is disabled and its developer tunnel is disconnected. No iOS 15 runtime is locally available. No TestFlight upload/processing/install, physical iPhone/iPad/widget/watch pass, or post-rollout crash evidence exists. The gate remains blocked.', 'Upload the exact retained IPA unchanged to TestFlight, install it on the ready iPhone and iPad, restore watch readiness, then run the complete iPhone/iPad/widget/watch matrix'),
    ('domain_activation', 'Domain activation', 'pass', 'At 2026-08-29 10:40–10:41 +05:00, authenticated GitHub Pages settings showed DNS check successful and Enforce HTTPS enabled. The Let''s Encrypt certificate has CN nimbo.uz, SANs nimbo.uz/www.nimbo.uz, and validates for both hosts. WHOIS, .uz delegation, authoritative Cloudflare records, and independent 1.1.1.1/8.8.8.8 resolution pass. HTTPS returns 200 with verification result 0 for all 12 published UZ-root/RU/EN landing, press, privacy, and support routes plus growth, robots, sitemap, and the valid metadata schema. HTTP apex redirects to HTTPS; HTTP www reaches HTTPS apex in two redirects; HTTPS www redirects directly to HTTPS apex. All 12 localized HTML routes have the expected HTTPS canonical and language. Uzbek intentionally uses ' || chr(47) || ' rather than a separate ' || chr(47) || 'uz' || chr(47) || ' route.', 'Maintain dated DNS, certificate, redirect, canonical, and localized-route verification at each release'),
    ('store_policy_console_clearance', 'Store policy console clearance', 'pass', 'The 2026-08-28 App Store read-only check found no open review/compliance action. Google Play reported no policy issues at 2026-08-29 13:12 +05:00; production remained active at 1.0.2 (6), 100%. At 13:59:40 +05:00, UZ Custom Store Listing 4834799756935529888 was saved only as Draft, not submitted for review or published; Publishing overview still showed the latest publication on 2026-08-27. This is point-in-time Console evidence, not a guarantee against later review. See growth/quality/store-policy-console-2026-08-28.md and growth/quality/google-play-console-2026-08-29.md.', 'Re-check both app-global store policy surfaces at the next evidence cutoff')
) AS gates(gate_id, gate, status, evidence, next_action);
